## What the official site says

[Rockstar’s GTA VI page](https://www.rockstargames.com/VI), checked on 13 November 2026, still says the game is coming November 19, 2026 for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S. The page now shows **Pre-Load Now**, and it still labels PlayStation 5 as the platform it plays best on. That page does not list a PC date.

Treat November 19 as Rockstar’s stated target, not a promise that the date cannot move. If it changes, the change belongs on Rockstar’s page.

This is a separate game from Grand Theft Auto V Enhanced, which is already released on PC. The Enhanced edition has its own [Steam listing](/apps/gta-v-enhanced).

## Who can pre-load now

Pre-loading is no longer a future November 10 start. Rockstar’s [Pre-Load Grand Theft Auto VI Now](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/89834o94713o21/pre-load-grand-theft-auto-vi-now) post, dated 10 November 2026 and still linked from the GTA VI page on 13 November 2026, says pre-loading is available for everyone who has pre-ordered digitally. The same post says players who pre-ordered the code-in-box version can activate that code and begin pre-loading as soon as the code is received.

| Platform | What the official sources say |
| --- | --- |
| PlayStation 5 | [PlayStation’s 10 November 2026 post](https://blog.playstation.com/2026/11/10/pre-load-grand-theft-auto-vi-on-ps5-starting-today/) says pre-loading is available at PlayStation Store. It also says code-in-box buyers can activate the code as soon as they get it. |
| Xbox Series X\|S | [Xbox Wire’s 10 November 2026 post](https://news.xbox.com/en-us/2026/11/10/grand-theft-auto-6-comes-to-xbox-cloud-gaming-november-19/) says Series X and Series S can pre-install now, and it asks players to begin early for launch day. |
| Xbox One | The same Xbox Wire post says Xbox One plays the game through Xbox Cloud Gaming on launch day. It does not describe a native Xbox One install. |
| PC | Rockstar’s GTA VI page still does not list a PC release. There is no PC pre-load to start from that page. |

Rockstar’s earlier [Pre-Load Begins on November 10](https://www.rockstargames.com/newswire/article/k4ak9okk485712) headline marked the start of that window. Use the newer **Pre-Load Now** post and your console store for the current download button.

## How release timing works

Rockstar’s page keeps November 19, 2026 as the launch day for PlayStation 5 and Xbox Series X|S.

PlayStation says launch unlocks on a rolling midnight by country, beginning at 12:00 a.m. NZDT in New Zealand on November 19 and continuing as other countries reach midnight. Pre-loading installs the game files early. It does not unlock play before that launch window.

Xbox Wire says cloud play for supported markets begins at 1 a.m. ET on November 19. A Series X or Series S native install is separate from cloud streaming.

[Rockstar’s platforms and editions support article](https://support.rockstargames.com/articles/4QfG4FmZCf5W1gS8jy4UVT/grand-theft-auto-vi-platform-editions-and-versions) says the physical version is a download code in a box, not a playable disc, and that those retail codes are meant to support pre-loading once received. Retail shipping and pickup timing can vary by store.

## What this page does not claim

This page does not quote a required download size. Rockstar’s current GTA VI page and the Pre-Load Now meta description checked here do not state a gigabyte figure, so none is invented.

This is a dated editorial snapshot. It is not a hands-on preview, a PC release date, or a performance comparison. GameNews is not affiliated with Rockstar. When a newer official post appears, use the publisher’s page rather than an older recap.
